<title>UK: BSkyB to end satellite deal with Kirch-FT.</title>
<headline>BSkyB to end satellite deal with Kirch-FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Sky Broadcasting, the satellite television company, and Kirch Gruppe, the German media group, will announce later on Friday that they have terminated their digital satellite joint venture agreement, the Financial Times said.</p>
<p>The paper said BSkyB and Kirch would cite failure to agree a number of fundamental issues as the reason for the mutual decision.</p>
<p>In July, BSkyB announced it was to take a 49 percent stake in DF1, Kirch's German digital television platform, said the paper.</p>
<p>News Corp Ltd owns 40 percent of BSkyB.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
